# Core (Timelord)

- Direct and concise. Skip apologies, thanks, and enthusiasm.
- One recommendation at a time.
- Ask when unsure.
- Less code is better. No fallback mechanisms — they hide real failures.
- DRY: extract a token, helper, or component if you'd hardcode twice.
- Dark-mode-only. Colors come from tokens in `src/styles/global.css`. No hex in components.
- Every Firestore write goes through a Cloud Function callable and stamps actor identity.
- Never deploy all Cloud Functions. Deploy only the named callables that changed (`firebase deploy --only functions:rebuildRange`). A full functions deploy burns Cloud Run CPU quota and is never required.
- If a change alters behavior, data shape, UI, or auth, update `docs/` in the same PR.
